  "mainEntity": {
    "name": "Are Motion Sensor Lights Right for Every Home?",
    "text": "Are Motion Sensor Lights Right for Every Home?",
    "@type": "Question",
    "answerCount": 1,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "text": "Motion sensor lights are super convenient and add a layer of security, but they aren't a one-size-fits-all solution for every home. When considering them, think about where you'd use them most. Indoors, they're great for areas like hallways, pantries, or even stairways where you only need light when someone's passing through. Outdoors, they boost security around entries, driveways, or side yards, activating only when movement is detected. A key question is how sensitive and far-reaching you need the detection to be. Do you want the lights to stay on all night with a dim glow, or only activate on approach? Compatibility is also big – ensure the sensor works with your chosen bulb or driver type, especially if you're going with LEDs or dimmers. And for outdoor installs, don't forget weatherproofing; wet-rated fixtures are a must where rain or snow can reach. If you're weighing the options or need help with a hard-wired setup, a professional can help you decide if motion sensor lighting is the perfect fit for your specific needs and ensure a smooth, compliant installation.",
      "@type": "Answer",
      "author": {
        "name": "HH Remodeling LLC",
        "@type": "Organization"
      }
    }
  }
